WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:05.160
In today’s video we are covering our first
Saint worshipped both by the Catholic and

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:10.230
Eastern Orthodox churches, revered for having
first introduced Christianity amongst the

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:11.230
Rus.

00:00:11.230 --> 00:00:15.769
These were a pagan people of Nordic descent,
who ruled over a vast land in the early Middle

00:00:15.769 --> 00:00:18.560
Ages, from the Baltic to the Black Sea.

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:23.800
But her holy title should not fool you, as
she did not dedicate her life solely to prayer

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:25.150
and converting the heathen.

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:29.560
This Saint was a ruler, the regent of the
Principality of Kiev, and one of the most

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:32.680
powerful women of the early Middle Ages.

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:37.340
Most of her life is lost to the shadows of
history, while the rest has emerged from the

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:38.570
mists of legend.

00:00:38.570 --> 00:00:45.050
In today’s Biographics, we will learn how
this widow of a Prince, with an infant son,

00:00:45.050 --> 00:00:50.970
defended her throne against insidious suitors,
hostile tribes and invading nomadic raiders.

00:00:50.970 --> 00:00:55.900
Most of all, we will hear about the incredible
story of how she avenged her husband with

00:00:55.900 --> 00:00:59.220
acts of escalating, ruthless cunning.

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:05.680
Please welcome today’s protagonist, Princess
Olga of Kiev.

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:18.730
The Kievan Rus
Before I begin the story of how Princess Olga

00:01:18.730 --> 00:01:21.960
defended her family and her lands, allow me
to give you some context.

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:25.210
Who were the Rus people and what lands did
they rule over?

00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:29.420
The Rus, sometimes also called Varangians,
were people of Scandinavian ethnicity who

00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:35.980
had founded the ‘Kievan Rus’ -- a political
federation that lasted from 862 to 1242.

00:01:35.980 --> 00:01:40.200
This state was located in modern-day Belarus,
Ukraine, and western Russia, which is actually

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:41.200
named after the Rus.

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:43.520
The capital city of this federation was Kiev,
in modern-day Ukraine.

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:48.840
`Kievan Rus’ can simply be translated as
“the lands of the Rus of Kiev”.

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:54.150
Their Scandinavian origin was first mentioned
by a Byzantine diplomat (and eventual Saint)

00:01:54.150 --> 00:01:59.360
named Bertin, who first recorded their presence
in his Annals of 839.

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:03.640
But most of the stories about the origin of
the Rus comes from the Primary Chronicle,

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:09.450
known also as the Tale of Bygone Years, an
early Russian text from the 12th Century.

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:14.060
According to the Chronicle, the original dwellers
of the area in the mid-ninth century had invited

00:02:14.060 --> 00:02:18.980
the Rus – described also as Vikings – to
rule and maintain order in their country.

00:02:18.980 --> 00:02:23.980
One of these Vikings was called Rurik, and
he founded his own dynasty, which ruled over

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:26.420
the area for more than seven centuries.

00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:32.700
The first Tsar of Russia -- Ivan IV, or Ivan
The Terrible -- was a direct descendant of

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:33.700
Rurik’s.

00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:39.160
The Kievan Rus, however, had ceased to exist
as a political entity long before Ivan.

00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:46.230
Between 1237 and 1242, the federation was
overrun by the unimpeded advance of the Mongol

00:02:46.230 --> 00:02:47.230
hordes!

00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:52.490
The federation was divided into smaller, disjointed
countries, which eventually evolved into Ukraine,

00:02:52.490 --> 00:02:53.880
Belarus and Russia.

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:59.370
But now, back to Rurik, as his bloodline is
directly involved in our main story today.

00:02:59.370 --> 00:03:03.430
At an unspecified time, in the second half
of the 9th Century, Rurik had established

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:09.520
his capital in Novgorod, and his men had begun
raiding the surrounding area, in true Viking

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:13.280
style, even going as far as attacking Constantinople.

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:18.760
When Rurik died of natural causes, his first-born
son Igor was too young to rule, and was put

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:21.880
under the care of Oleg of Novgorod.

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:27.150
After more campaigns to conquer and consolidate
territories around Novgorod, Oleg moved the

00:03:27.150 --> 00:03:33.030
capital to Kiev, to seize the enormous wealth
amassed by two former allies of Rurik.

00:03:33.030 --> 00:03:36.980
In 912, Oleg died, and in a very interesting
way, too.

00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:41.640
A prophecy had foretold him that his favourite
horse would be the cause of his death.

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:46.901
Oleg, a superstitious man, had made sure the
horse was cared for as far as possible away

00:03:46.901 --> 00:03:47.901
from him.

00:03:47.901 --> 00:03:51.700
When he heard that the horse had died, Oleg
considered himself freed of the curse, and

00:03:51.700 --> 00:03:54.430
mockingly kicked at the poor animal’s skull.

00:03:54.430 --> 00:03:59.780
He chose poorly: a snake beneath the carcass
was startled, bit Oleg on the foot, and killed

00:03:59.780 --> 00:04:00.780
him.

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:04.620
In the meantime, Igor had come of age, and
so he ascended to the throne, formally becoming

00:04:04.620 --> 00:04:06.420
Prince Igor of Kiev.

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:10.940
By this time, he had already married a Varangian
Lady named Olga.

00:04:10.940 --> 00:04:18.539
The Slaying of a Prince
Following in the footsteps of his father and

00:04:18.539 --> 00:04:23.719
his guardian, Igor continued engaging in successful
conquests, raiding the neighbouring territories

00:04:23.719 --> 00:04:26.909
and exacting heavy tributes to fill his coffers.

00:04:26.909 --> 00:04:29.690
But Igor was greedy, and he wanted more.

00:04:29.690 --> 00:04:35.029
In 945, he considered paying a visit to the
land of the Drevlians, a local tribe which

00:04:35.029 --> 00:04:39.849
had been an ally to Rurik, joining his raiders
in attacks against the Byzantine Empire.

00:04:39.849 --> 00:04:44.990
Later, the Drevlians had paid tribute to Oleg,
but had stopped when he had kicked the horse’s

00:04:44.990 --> 00:04:45.990
head.

00:04:45.990 --> 00:04:50.520
Since then, the Drevlians had paid what was
effectively protection money to a rival landlord.

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:56.599
Igor saw this as a perfect occasion to collect
some late payments and set off on his mission.

00:04:56.599 --> 00:05:00.969
According to the Primary Chronicle, he raided
the land of Dereva and collected his tribute

00:05:00.969 --> 00:05:01.969
by violence.

00:05:01.969 --> 00:05:07.080
But on his way back to Kiev, he still felt
a thirst for more gold and riches.

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:10.490
He ordered his men to return home, except
for a few followers.

00:05:10.490 --> 00:05:15.939
With them in tow, he rode back to the Drevlians
“desirous of still greater booty.”

00:05:15.939 --> 00:05:19.240
Like Oleg, he had tried his luck once too
many.

00:05:19.240 --> 00:05:23.350
His returning party was spotted by the Drevlians,
who reported back to their leader, Prince

00:05:23.350 --> 00:05:24.350
Mal.

00:05:24.350 --> 00:05:28.759
The Prince had had enough, proclaiming,
"If a wolf come among the sheep, he will take

00:05:28.759 --> 00:05:32.650
away the whole flock one by one, unless he
be killed.

00:05:32.650 --> 00:05:36.159
If we do not thus kill him now, he will destroy
us all."

00:05:36.159 --> 00:05:41.210
The Drevlian warriors then rode forth from
their city of Iskorosten, massacred Igor’s

00:05:41.210 --> 00:05:44.300
soldiers and reserved for him a gruesome execution.

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:49.120
I will leave the description to Byzantine
chronicler Leo the Deacon:

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:53.949
“They had bent down two birch trees to the
prince’s feet and tied them to his legs.”

00:05:53.949 --> 00:05:56.029
And then:
“They let the trees straighten again, thus

00:05:56.029 --> 00:05:58.659
tearing the prince’s body apart.”

00:05:58.659 --> 00:06:02.120
With this threat disposed of, the Drevlians
planned their counterattack.

00:06:02.120 --> 00:06:05.860
They would take over Kiev itself, not by conquest,
but by marriage.

00:06:05.860 --> 00:06:09.920
Prince Mal ordered for some emissaries to
visit the now widowed Olga to ask for her

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:10.920
hand in marriage.

00:06:10.920 --> 00:06:16.310
It is not clear if this was a common habit
at the time, or if Mal was simply very arrogant.

00:06:16.310 --> 00:06:21.099
Back in her capital, Olga awaited for Igor’s
return in vain.

00:06:21.099 --> 00:06:26.009
By her side, she had her boy son Svyatoslav,
who too young to fight, let alone rule.

00:06:26.009 --> 00:06:30.499
Mal’s idea was that by becoming his stepfather,
he could influence the little prince into

00:06:30.499 --> 00:06:31.830
doing his own bidding.

00:06:31.830 --> 00:06:36.680
So the delegation of the Drevlians sailed
a boat along the river Dnipro.

00:06:36.680 --> 00:06:41.039
Mal had sent twenty of his best advisors to
put forward his proposal, clearly believing

00:06:41.039 --> 00:06:43.300
they would be welcomed with open arms.

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:48.289
This is when the Primary Chronicle, and our
own story, centres on Olga.

00:06:48.289 --> 00:06:53.110
The Princess sent her own emissaries to ask
for the reason of the Drevlians’ visit.

00:06:53.110 --> 00:06:55.919
They announced that they had slain her husband,
because

00:06:55.919 --> 00:07:01.869
“He was like a wolf, crafty and ravening”
but that Prince Mal was a good leader and

00:07:01.869 --> 00:07:05.509
that Olga should come to the land of Dereva
and marry him.

00:07:05.509 --> 00:07:07.999
Olga’s reply was what the delegation was
expected.

00:07:07.999 --> 00:07:12.349
In fact, she said that their proposal was
pleasing to her ears, but asked for the delegates

00:07:12.349 --> 00:07:16.090
to wait on their boat, and that they would
be picked up the following morning.

00:07:16.090 --> 00:07:20.389
As the twenty Drevlians waited, Olga had the
hall of her castle prepared to give them their

00:07:20.389 --> 00:07:21.770
deserved welcome.

00:07:21.770 --> 00:07:26.259
The morning after, when the Rus came to collect
the Drevlians, the latter demanded to be carried

00:07:26.259 --> 00:07:28.399
into the castle in their own boat.

00:07:28.399 --> 00:07:32.270
The Rus complied, as this was the same order
they had received from Olga.

00:07:32.270 --> 00:07:36.020
When they arrived in the castle, they found
what surprise lay waiting for them: during

00:07:36.020 --> 00:07:40.659
the night, the Princess had commanded for
a large, deep ditch to be dug within the castle

00:07:40.659 --> 00:07:41.659
walls.

00:07:41.659 --> 00:07:45.449
The Drevlians did not have time to react,
as the Rus hurled them, boat and all, inside

00:07:45.449 --> 00:07:46.449
the trench.

00:07:46.449 --> 00:07:51.469
The delegates protested to no avail, as Olga
ordered that they be buried alive.

00:07:51.469 --> 00:07:55.759
With her simple trap, the Princess had wiped
out a large part of the enemy leadership.

00:07:55.759 --> 00:07:57.711
That was only the beginning of her revenge.

00:07:57.711 --> 00:08:06.409
A Feast of Mead
Prince Mal was unaware of what had happened

00:08:06.409 --> 00:08:10.379
in Kiev, so he was not suspicious of the message
he received from Olga.

00:08:10.379 --> 00:08:15.369
She insisted that she was eager to meet, but
she would do so only if Mal sent more of his

00:08:15.369 --> 00:08:17.300
own distinguished men to pick her up.

00:08:17.300 --> 00:08:21.779
The Prince, who it is safe to say, was quite
a gullible man, agreed to it, and gathered

00:08:21.779 --> 00:08:26.539
more of his chieftains, warriors, and advisors
to pay homage to the Rus Princess.

00:08:26.539 --> 00:08:31.209
When this second delegation arrived in Kiev,
Olga demanded that they bathe before she would

00:08:31.209 --> 00:08:32.510
give them audience.

00:08:32.510 --> 00:08:37.150
The Drevlians, surely tired, sweaty and covered
in dirt from the journey, eagerly complied

00:08:37.150 --> 00:08:39.550
and entered the bathhouse that had been readied.

00:08:39.550 --> 00:08:44.800
As they relaxed inside the sauna, they were
startled by a sharp noise: somebody was locking

00:08:44.800 --> 00:08:46.410
the bathhouse doors from outside.

00:08:46.410 --> 00:08:48.510
Their attempts to force their way out were
futile.

00:08:48.510 --> 00:08:52.020
In horror, they heard Olga’s stern voice
through the wooden doors.

00:08:52.020 --> 00:08:55.100
She had just given orders to set the house
on fire.

00:08:55.100 --> 00:09:00.250
First by earth, then by fire, the Princess
regent had sealed her first two murderous

00:09:00.250 --> 00:09:05.850
campaigns against the enemy tribe, with their
leadership almost entirely decapitated.

00:09:05.850 --> 00:09:08.000
But she wasn’t done yet.

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:11.910
Before Mal could become suspicious of the
long absence of his men, she sent another

00:09:11.910 --> 00:09:14.330
message:
"I am now coming to you, so prepare great

00:09:14.330 --> 00:09:19.640
quantities of mead in the city where you killed
my husband, that I may weep over his grave

00:09:19.640 --> 00:09:21.580
and hold a funeral feast for him."

00:09:21.580 --> 00:09:26.600
Mead was a popular alcoholic beverage in medieval
times, made with fermented honey and water.

00:09:26.600 --> 00:09:31.010
When they received the message, the Drevlians
set to work, preparing gallons of mead and

00:09:31.010 --> 00:09:32.120
a lavish feast.

00:09:32.120 --> 00:09:35.970
Olga arrived shortly thereafter, with a small
escort in tow.

00:09:35.970 --> 00:09:40.300
She arrived at Igor’s tomb and asked her
men to build a funeral mound, around which

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:42.770
the Drevlians gathered for the funeral feast.

00:09:42.770 --> 00:09:47.000
Some Drevlian who was smarter than the others
asked what had become of the two delegations

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:51.500
they had already sent, to which the sly Olga
replied that they were on their way, escorted

00:09:51.500 --> 00:09:53.560
by her late husband’s guard of honour.

00:09:53.560 --> 00:09:58.130
With the Drevlian judgment clouded by the
rivers of freely flowing mead, they swallowed

00:09:58.130 --> 00:09:59.170
the lie easily.

00:09:59.170 --> 00:10:03.900
Olga asked her men to wait upon the Drevlians,
ensuring their cups were never empty.

00:10:03.900 --> 00:10:09.270
She waited patiently until they were all drunk
and at her signal, the massacre started.

00:10:09.270 --> 00:10:13.440
Taken by surprise, her enemies fell one by
one under the blades of the Rus.

00:10:13.440 --> 00:10:19.220
According to the Chronicle, five thousand
Drevlians were cut down at the Red Funeral.

00:10:19.220 --> 00:10:26.060
Revenge Is a Dish Best Served on Fire
A five-thousand man massacre still was not

00:10:26.060 --> 00:10:27.060
quite enough.

00:10:27.060 --> 00:10:29.900
Olga was bent on complete, total reprisal.

00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:33.590
Again moving swiftly, the Princess returned
to Kiev and gathered her army.

00:10:33.590 --> 00:10:37.900
The boy Prince Svyatoslav joined his mother,
and together, they marched back to the land

00:10:37.900 --> 00:10:38.900
of Dereva.

00:10:38.900 --> 00:10:43.010
He was just a child, but when his troops made
contact with the enemy, Svyatoslav was the

00:10:43.010 --> 00:10:45.360
first to cast a spear from atop his horse.

00:10:45.360 --> 00:10:49.440
His arms were obviously too weak, and the
spear barely cleared the horse's ears.

00:10:49.440 --> 00:10:54.050
Regardless, Olga’s Generals, Sveinald and
Asmund, proudly announced that the prince

00:10:54.050 --> 00:10:58.090
had already begun battle, and pressed the
vassals to follow his example.

00:10:58.090 --> 00:11:01.880
The Rus charged forward and completely routed
the Drevlians.

00:11:01.880 --> 00:11:05.390
The surviving men, women and children of the
unfortunate tribe sought refuge within the

00:11:05.390 --> 00:11:07.490
walls of their main city, Iskorosten.

00:11:07.490 --> 00:11:12.840
Olga and her troops besieged the city, but
the Drevlians valiantly repelled their assaults.

00:11:12.840 --> 00:11:17.630
They knew that this was a fight for their
own existence and would resist to the bitter

00:11:17.630 --> 00:11:18.630
end.

00:11:18.630 --> 00:11:22.820
In the meanwhile, other towns and cities of
their land had capitulated, and were now living

00:11:22.820 --> 00:11:24.380
in relative peace with the Rus.

00:11:24.380 --> 00:11:26.450
They were of course, paying their tribute!

00:11:26.450 --> 00:11:31.290
After one year, Iskorosten still stood firm,
and Olga had to think of another plan to resolve

00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:32.290
the stalemate.

00:11:32.290 --> 00:11:35.170
One day, the besieged citizens received a
message from the Princess:

00:11:35.170 --> 00:11:37.850
"Why do you persist in holding out?

00:11:37.850 --> 00:11:41.930
All your cities have surrendered to me and
submitted to tribute, so that the inhabitants

00:11:41.930 --> 00:11:44.710
now cultivate their fields and lands in peace.

00:11:44.710 --> 00:11:48.760
But you had rather die of hunger, without
submitting to tribute."

00:11:48.760 --> 00:11:52.300
The Derevlians started to buckle and replied
that they would be glad to pay tribute, but

00:11:52.300 --> 00:11:55.630
that they could not trust her, as she was
still determined to avenge Igor.

00:11:55.630 --> 00:12:00.410
Olga was apparently relieved to start negotiations
with the defenders and let them know that

00:12:00.410 --> 00:12:06.680
she considered her slain husband to have been
already avenged, not once, not twice, but

00:12:06.680 --> 00:12:07.680
thrice.

00:12:07.680 --> 00:12:12.380
After all, she had already massacred two delegations,
plus those who had attended the funeral feast.

00:12:12.380 --> 00:12:16.900
In order to seal the peace, she demanded one
last, small tribute from the Drevlians, after

00:12:16.900 --> 00:12:18.490
which she would return home.

00:12:18.490 --> 00:12:23.170
Olga’s request was surprisingly modest,
as she realised that the city had been impoverished

00:12:23.170 --> 00:12:28.100
by the siege: she only wanted three sparrows
and three pigeons from each house.

00:12:28.100 --> 00:12:29.900
The Drevlians were elated.

00:12:29.900 --> 00:12:34.270
They collected the small flocks of six birds
from every household and sent them to Olga,

00:12:34.270 --> 00:12:36.830
who promised to lift the siege the following
morning.

00:12:36.830 --> 00:12:41.280
This was the last act of Olga’s plan of
total revenge and annihilation.

00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:45.740
If one year of frontal assaults and siege
engines could not achieve victory, the intellect

00:12:45.740 --> 00:12:47.580
of a Princess definitely could.

00:12:47.580 --> 00:12:54.280
And she would so by turning innocent, harmless,
pet birds into a weapon of mass destruction.

00:12:54.280 --> 00:12:58.300
She ordered her soldiers to take one bird
each and to attach to their talons a piece

00:12:58.300 --> 00:13:00.560
of sulphur, bound in cloth.

00:13:00.560 --> 00:13:03.670
When night fell, the soldiers released the
sparrows, and the pigeons.

00:13:03.670 --> 00:13:06.750
Their silent wings carried them back to their
nests, their dove-cotes, under the eaves of

00:13:06.750 --> 00:13:07.750
their homes.

00:13:07.750 --> 00:13:11.850
One by one, the houses of Iskorosten were
lit by fires.

00:13:11.850 --> 00:13:16.610
Soon, the whole city was burning, its inhabitants
either killed in their sleep or running in

00:13:16.610 --> 00:13:19.190
terror, unable to extinguish the flames.

00:13:19.190 --> 00:13:23.220
Some of them fled outside the city walls,
but they were quickly seized by Olga’s soldiers.

00:13:23.220 --> 00:13:27.440
She kept the elders captive, had some of the
others sold as slave, and many more were killed

00:13:27.440 --> 00:13:28.460
on the spot.

00:13:28.460 --> 00:13:32.440
This was the final and total triumph of Princess
Olga of Kiev, victor of Iskorosten, scourge

00:13:32.440 --> 00:13:33.440
of the Drevlians, Mother of Sparrows.

00:13:33.440 --> 00:13:34.440
[Note to the Team: I liked the idea of giving
her a string of titles like another vengeful

00:13:34.440 --> 00:13:35.440
Queen of a popular series of books and TV
shows.

00:13:35.440 --> 00:13:36.440
Victor of Iskorosten is quite logical.

00:13:36.440 --> 00:13:37.970
Scourge of the Drevlians I heard it on a podcast
about her revenge story, but it did not have

00:13:37.970 --> 00:13:38.970
source.

00:13:38.970 --> 00:13:39.970
But again, difficult to argue with.

00:13:39.970 --> 00:13:41.920
Mother of Sparrows, is a title I gave her
myself, which I think sounds good and ties

00:13:41.920 --> 00:13:44.070
back to that other Queen, who despite her
dragons wasn’t half as effective]

00:13:44.070 --> 00:13:47.880
A New Faith
In the following years, until 948, Olga continued

00:13:47.880 --> 00:13:51.350
to act as regent for her boy prince Vyaroslav.

00:13:51.350 --> 00:13:55.370
The Drevlians had been completely subdued
and paid regular tribute to the Rus.

00:13:55.370 --> 00:13:58.480
The Principality was at peace and grew prosperous.

00:13:58.480 --> 00:14:03.880
Finally, the Princess set on a journey to
Constantinople, or as the Rus called it, Tasr’grad,

00:14:03.880 --> 00:14:05.380
the City of Caesars.

00:14:05.380 --> 00:14:10.010
The Chronicle does not offer a reason for
this visit, but we can assume it was of a

00:14:10.010 --> 00:14:11.010
diplomatic nature.

00:14:11.010 --> 00:14:16.400
The Rus and the Byzantine Empire had a love-hate
relationship, characterised by raids and attacks

00:14:16.400 --> 00:14:21.070
by both sides, but also by trade and occasional
cooperation.

00:14:21.070 --> 00:14:26.690
It was during this period that Byzantine Emperors
actually started to recruit Rus warriors in

00:14:26.690 --> 00:14:28.410
their elite Varangian guard.

00:14:28.410 --> 00:14:33.910
In 948, the Emperor was Constantine VII, who
upon meeting Olga, immediately took a liking

00:14:33.910 --> 00:14:34.910
to her.

00:14:34.910 --> 00:14:39.770
Impressed by her beauty and intellect, Constantine
remarked that she was worthy to reign with

00:14:39.770 --> 00:14:40.770
him.

00:14:40.770 --> 00:14:45.810
We have learned by now that Olga did not take
well to suitors, but in this case, her reaction

00:14:45.810 --> 00:14:48.500
was… well, less violent, at least.

00:14:48.500 --> 00:14:53.930
The Princess did not outright reject the proposal,
but simply stated that being a pagan, she

00:14:53.930 --> 00:14:55.940
could not marry a Christian monarch.

00:14:55.940 --> 00:14:59.140
But, if he really insisted, he could baptize
her.

00:14:59.140 --> 00:15:04.190
The Emperor agreed, and with the assistance
of the Patriarch of Constantinople, had her

00:15:04.190 --> 00:15:06.160
converted into the Christian Orthodox faith.

00:15:06.160 --> 00:15:10.060
The Chronicle reports that Olga accepted very
eagerly the teachings of the Church

00:15:10.060 --> 00:15:12.440
“like a sponge absorbing water.”

00:15:12.440 --> 00:15:16.930
At her baptism, she was christened Helena,
and the Emperor acted as her godfather at

00:15:16.930 --> 00:15:18.400
her own insistence.

00:15:18.400 --> 00:15:20.930
-
After receiving the sacrament, Olga, or Helena,

00:15:20.930 --> 00:15:23.750
was summoned by Constantine who renewed his
proposal.

00:15:23.750 --> 00:15:27.530
There were no obstacles now; she should become
his wife!

00:15:27.530 --> 00:15:29.730
But she replied that this was not possible.

00:15:29.730 --> 00:15:35.360
He was her godfather, after all, which made
her his daughter in the eye of the church.

00:15:35.360 --> 00:15:38.640
It was unlawful for a man to marry his own
daughter!

00:15:38.640 --> 00:15:41.050
The Emperor considered her reply, then simply
said

00:15:41.050 --> 00:15:42.970
"Olga, you have outwitted me."

00:15:42.970 --> 00:15:47.750
He then covered her in gifts, gold, silver,
and silks, and bade her farewell.

00:15:47.750 --> 00:15:51.620
Olga had barely returned to Kiev when she
received a message from the Emperor.

00:15:51.620 --> 00:15:56.750
Apparently, those gifts were not entirely
for free and he expected slaves, wax, furs

00:15:56.750 --> 00:15:57.860
and mercenaries in return.

00:15:57.860 --> 00:15:58.860
What a cheapo.

00:15:58.860 --> 00:16:03.710
Olga was unfazed and simply replied to the
Byzantine envoy that she would pay back her

00:16:03.710 --> 00:16:10.060
due only if the Caesar was willing to spend
as much time in Kiev as she had spent in Constantinople.

00:16:10.060 --> 00:16:14.720
It is not recorded whether the Emperor paid
her a visit, so we will assume he didn’t

00:16:14.720 --> 00:16:16.960
… and she had outwitted him again!

00:16:16.960 --> 00:16:22.010
Now, as a recently converted Christian, Olga
tried to spread her new-found religion amongst

00:16:22.010 --> 00:16:24.339
her people, starting with her own son.

00:16:24.339 --> 00:16:29.130
But Prince Svyatoslav was not convinced, fearing
he would be mocked by his subjects if he did

00:16:29.130 --> 00:16:30.130
so.

00:16:30.130 --> 00:16:33.921
Olga accepted this refusal as her only defeat
so far, but according to the Chronicle, she

00:16:33.921 --> 00:16:39.350
prayed day and night for God to forgive the
heathen souls of Svyatoslav and the Rus.

00:16:39.350 --> 00:16:44.460
By 956 Prince Svyatoslav had come of age,
and, hungry for conquest, he built a valiant

00:16:44.460 --> 00:16:48.110
army and set off on several lengthy campaigns
away from Kiev.

00:16:48.110 --> 00:16:52.180
While he was away, the land of the Rus was
invaded by the Pechenegs, a nomadic tribe.

00:16:52.180 --> 00:16:55.160
They swept through the country and eventually
attacked Kiev.

00:16:55.160 --> 00:16:59.600
Olga shut herself up in the city with her
grandsons, Yaropolk, Oleg, and Vladimir.

00:16:59.600 --> 00:17:02.330
Now it was her turn to be under siege.

00:17:02.330 --> 00:17:06.569
The only chance of survival for the Kievans
was to send a message to a relief force, on

00:17:06.569 --> 00:17:08.189
the other side of the river Dnipro.

00:17:08.189 --> 00:17:11.839
A clever boy, whose name was never recorded,
volunteered for the sortie.

00:17:11.839 --> 00:17:16.059
He could speak the language of the Pechenegs
and so he simply walked out of the city with

00:17:16.059 --> 00:17:20.669
a bridle in his hand, asking the nomadic riders
if anybody had seen his horse.

00:17:20.669 --> 00:17:24.589
The ruse worked and he was able to jump into
the river and swim to the other shore.

00:17:24.589 --> 00:17:28.730
The relief army soon arrived and their general,
called Pretich, convinced the leader of the

00:17:28.730 --> 00:17:33.940
Pechenegs that his was just the vanguard of
a massive army led by Vyaroslav.

00:17:33.940 --> 00:17:38.440
These Rus were crafty people, indeed, and
all their foes were a bunch of yokels, apparently:

00:17:38.440 --> 00:17:41.210
the Pechenegs bought the lie and agreed to
a truce.

00:17:41.210 --> 00:17:45.639
In the meanwhile, Olga had sent a messenger
to recall the Prince, who returned in time

00:17:45.639 --> 00:17:49.451
to decisively drive the Pechenegs back into
the steppes.

00:17:49.451 --> 00:17:53.900
For many years Svyatoslav remained in Kiev,
finally fulfilling his duties of ruler, in

00:17:53.900 --> 00:17:56.619
addition to his early honors as a conqueror.

00:17:56.619 --> 00:18:02.480
But in 969 he announced to his mother and
his advisors, the boyars, that he had no intention

00:18:02.480 --> 00:18:04.019
to remain in Kiev anymore.

00:18:04.019 --> 00:18:08.230
During his earlier campaigns, he had established
his base in the city of Pereyaslavets, where

00:18:08.230 --> 00:18:13.610
all his riches were concentrated:
" Gold, silks, wine, and various fruits from

00:18:13.610 --> 00:18:18.869
Greece, silver and horses from Hungary and
Bohemia, and from Rus furs, wax, honey, and

00:18:18.869 --> 00:18:19.899
slaves."

00:18:19.899 --> 00:18:21.700
If that was the truth, he had a point.

00:18:21.700 --> 00:18:24.409
But Olga was sad to see him depart once again.

00:18:24.409 --> 00:18:29.269
Now aged 70, the Princess was in poor health
and begged him first to await her death, and

00:18:29.269 --> 00:18:30.570
then go wherever he would like.

00:18:30.570 --> 00:18:33.270
The Prince yielded, but he did not have to
wait long.

00:18:33.270 --> 00:18:36.110
Three days after Olga had made her plea, she
died.

00:18:36.110 --> 00:18:40.000
Her son, her grandsons, and all of her people
wept for her in mourning.

00:18:40.000 --> 00:18:44.360
Olga had given command not to hold a funeral
feast for her, as was part of the pagan traditions.

00:18:44.360 --> 00:18:49.289
Instead, she had called for a Christian priest
to perform the last rites in a subdued ceremony.

00:18:49.289 --> 00:18:53.220
It was her grandson Vladimir the Great who
eventually converted all of the Kievan Rus

00:18:53.220 --> 00:18:58.809
to the Orthodox faith, but Olga was hailed
by later generations as Equal among the Apostles,

00:18:58.809 --> 00:19:02.869
for her role as a precursor to the widespread
introduction of Christianity.

00:19:02.869 --> 00:19:07.190
In the Primary Chronicle, it is written that
she was as the dawn that precedes the day.

00:19:07.190 --> 00:19:12.289
“She shone like the moon by night, and she
was radiant among the infidels like a pearl

00:19:12.289 --> 00:19:13.289
in the mire.

00:19:13.289 --> 00:19:17.880
She was the first from Rus to enter the kingdom
of God, and the sons of Rus thus praise her

00:19:17.880 --> 00:19:23.429
as their leader, for since her death she has
interceded with God in their behalf.”

00:19:23.429 --> 00:19:28.320
Princess Olga of Kiev was canonized in 1547,
officially becoming Saint Olga.

00:19:28.320 --> 00:19:33.070
She is probably the only mass murderering
Saint in history, but I may be wrong.

00:19:33.070 --> 00:19:37.280
Other monarchs and Popes have been canonized
over the centuries, and these rulers can rarely

00:19:37.280 --> 00:19:41.110
have a career without getting their hands
at least a little bit bloody.

00:19:41.110 --> 00:19:43.419
So, I hope you liked today’s video.

00:19:43.419 --> 00:19:47.119
As I mentioned at the start, it is difficult
to discern which parts of Olga’s life belong

00:19:47.119 --> 00:19:51.029
to the realm of history, and which to the
realm of myth.

00:19:51.029 --> 00:19:55.470
What parts do you think were true and what
parts do you believe were medieval propaganda?

00:19:55.470 --> 00:20:00.239
Please comment, share and subscribe … and
as usual, thank you for watching!

